# Berlin.rb

> Berlin.rb is a monthly Ruby meetup for the Berlin Ruby community, on the second Tuesday of every month: talks, project show-and-tells and casual get-togethers. Free and open to everyone.

Every talk and meetup page has a Markdown version: the page's address with `.md` in place of its trailing slash, as linked below. Recorded talks include chapters and a summary of the talk. All of them are in one file at <%= Berlinrb::Site::ORIGIN %>/llms-full.txt.

## Talks

<%- site.talks_newest_first.each do |talk| -%>
- [<%= talk["title"] %>](<%= site.markdown_url(site.talk_path(talk)) %>): by <%= talk["speaker"] %>, Berlin.rb #<%= talk["meetup"]["number"] %>, <%= site.short_date(talk["meetup"]["date"]) %><%= ", upcoming" if site.upcoming?(talk["meetup"]) %><%= ", recorded" if talk["video"] %>
<%- end -%>

## Meetups

<%- site.meetups.reverse_each do |meetup| -%>
- [Berlin.rb #<%= meetup["number"] %>](<%= site.markdown_url(site.meetup_path(meetup)) %>): <%= site.short_date(meetup["date"]) %><%= ", #{meetup["venue"]}" if meetup["venue"] %>
<%- end -%>

## Get involved

- [Give a talk, host or sponsor](<%= Berlinrb::Site::ORIGIN %>/get-involved/): propose a talk, or offer your office or support for a meetup
- [Luma calendar](https://luma.com/berlinrb): sign up for upcoming meetups

## Optional

- [Press kit](<%= Berlinrb::Site::ORIGIN %>/press/): logos and a short description of Berlin.rb
